{
 "row": "E81",
 "experiment": "the engines under signals (sp3/CLI/sigdrive.py, wsl_sig.sh, wsl_sig2.sh)",
 "result": "each engine in its own session, signalled after 3 s (VACASK) or 6 s (Xyce): SIGINT, TERM, HUP, QUIT, USR1, USR2 end it within 0.00-0.01 s (rc -2, -15, -1, -3, -10, -12); after fix_points the rawfiles hold 1,564,664-1,655,032 (VACASK) and 285,184-304,128 (Xyce) points; a VACASK started with & from a non-interactive bash (SIGINT inherited as SIG_IGN) still ran 5 min 14 s after kill -INT; under nohup, signal.getsignal(SIGHUP) is SIG_IGN (1), without it 0 (TestE81Dispositions)",
 "rules": [
  "\u00a72.7 signals: SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGQUIT forwarded to the engine stop it at once, leaving a readable rawfile after fix_points; SIGUSR1/2 are never forwarded because each kills both engines; a signal that was ignored at start stays ignored"
 ],
